    "narrative": "The Austin Waves are positioned for a high-ceiling outing today, headlined by **Gunnar Henderson** (81.88) and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (81.21). Both players benefit from favorable matchups against right-handed starters Yesavage and Young, respectively. **Gunnar Henderson**\u2019s aggressive order placement in the two-hole, combined with a strong park factor, makes him the premier anchor of the lineup. Similarly, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** capitalizes on a high xwOBA environment against Young; while the dynamic platoon split shows a slight negative, his raw power profile against a pitcher with an xERA approaching 5.00 makes him our highest-impact play for counting stats. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (70.03) rounds out our top-tier targets, leveraging a significant platoon advantage against King, M to provide reliable production.\n\nDecisions on the fringes were dictated by our extreme valuation of stolen base efficiency, which left **Coby Mayo** (48.93) on the bench despite his strong park-adjusted projection. While **Coby Mayo** is a high-upside asset, the optimizer prioritized the positional flexibility and defensive security of **Miguel Andujar** (57.21), who benefits from a +12% dynamic platoon edge today. Our biggest risk remains the slate of left-handed starters, particularly Luzardo, which drags the projected scores for **Kyle Tucker** (52.47), **Andy Pages** (47.29), and **Jackson Merrill** (47.28) toward the marginal threshold. We are monitoring **Andy Pages** closely, as the combination of an elite catcher\u2019s pop time and the pitcher\u2019s ability to hold runners limits his SB potential, essentially neutralizing the scarcest asset in our 5x5 framework. **Jorge Polanco** remains unavailable due to his IL designation, removing him from consideration as we look to maximize efficiency across our remaining active roster.",
